  "hints": [
    "Only expand elements when isinstance(item, list). Leave strings, numbers, tuples, and dicts intact.",
    "You can walk recursively into sublists or iterate explicitly with a stack for arbitrary nesting depth.",
    "Pseudocode (recursive):\n  out = []\n  for item in nested:\n      if isinstance(item, list): out.extend(flatten_list(item))\n      else: out.append(item)\n  return out"
